    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Describe your issue\n\nFused functions spend a lot of time in `__pyx_FusedFunction_call()` packing tuples. It should be replaced by an implementation based on the vectorcall protocol.",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I'd like to work on this. Plan: give the fused function type a vectorcall slot, select the specialisation directly from the args/kwnames array instead of packing a tuple in `__pyx_FusedFunction_call()`, forward to the chosen CyFunction with vectorcall, and keep the `tp_call` path for the Limited API. I'll add tests under tests/run/fused_* and a small benchmark. Does that match what you had in mind?",
            "created_at": "2026-10-09T16:29:49Z",
